## 3. Analysis of Items #9 (`skip_barrier`) and #10 / K2 (Wave/LDS Occupancy A/B)

- **Item #9 (`skip_barrier` outside `flow`)**:
  - In `Engine::record_net` (`gpu/src/engine.cpp:567-572`), the only two independent consecutive dispatches (`pooled_history2` writing `pdst_` and `ae` writing `expo_[cur]`/`blk_`) already omit the UAV barrier between them (`d.barrier()` is issued only after `ae`).
  - All other dispatches outside the 10-kernel `enc2..dec2_1` flow chain (`enc0_attr -> enc0_stage_32_64 -> enc1`, and `dec2_1 -> dec1_0 -> dec1_1 -> dec0_0 -> dec0_1 -> post -> downsample`) have strict full-tensor RAW dependencies on the immediately preceding kernel's output buffer; skipping any of those UAV barriers would cause data races.
- **Item #10 / K2 (Top-5 hottest dispatches & `occ_pad` LDS occupancy A/B)**:
  - At both 1080p Quality (`1280x720 -> 1920x1080`) and 4K Quality (`2560x1440 -> 3840x2160`), the Top-5 dispatches account for ~53.5%–55.9% of total GPU time: `enc0_stage_32_64` (~12.4–12.8%), `post` (~11.4–12.5%), `dec_up_32_64_64` (~10.7–11.1%), `dec_head_32_64` (~10.3–10.7%), and `enc_stage_64_64_96` (~8.6–8.7%).
  - Testing 16 KB LDS occupancy padding (`LDS_OCC_PAD=8192` / `POST_OCC_PAD=4096`, capping WGP occupancy to 4 WGs/WGP) against baseline (`diff_words=0/8294400`, 100% bit-exact):
    - On the three `W1` (`C=32`, 1 wave32/WG) network kernels (`enc0_stage_32_64_f_lt`, `dec_up_32_64_64_f_lt`, `dec_head_32_64_f_lt`), `LDS_OCC_PAD=8192` reduces L0/MALL cache thrashing and speeds up median execution by `-2.8%`, `-4.6%`, and `-4.8%` respectively.
    - On `post_f_lt` (`-0.1%`, noise) and `W2` `enc_stage_64_64_96_f_lt` (`+2.3%` slower; already tuned to 9.5 KB / 6 WGs per CU in `onr_block.glsl:342`), additional LDS padding has no benefit or slightly regresses.
